{
  "dom_id": "step-e5719",
  "name": "Example: Identifying a Diagram Corresponding to a Model",
  "problem": "Which of the following scatter plots shows a possible exponential dependence between the variables?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226611/assets/33343af118a165da06ca7e361088bad26a7ced2b0039179822fe046d9ffd761b.png)",
  "worked_solution": "In the case of exponential dependence, the points on the plot should be scattered along a curve whose $y$-values increase or decrease rapidly.\n\nAmong the given options, the only scatter plot that fits the description is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226611/assets/fc96819983d673d889cbf8be48e92f4546010640d555d1b41074fd031cf4430d.png)",
